"""Alberto Fussar, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 4 and 5, epilogue 1907).

Fussar appears only in Red Dead Redemption 2. Nothing in Red Dead Redemption (1911-1914) or Undead Nightmare mentions
him: no h3 for those periods.

SOURCE REGISTER (fetched Oct 2026; wiki pages cached in scripts/v3/work/_m/, other material in scripts/v3/work/fussar/fc/):
- Red Dead Wiki EN "Alberto Fussar" (scripts/v3/work/fussar/en.txt): History (Background, Saint Denis Chapter, Guarma
  Chapter), Personality, Appearance, Mission appearances, Quotes, Trivia, Gallery captions. Red Dead Wiki FR "Alberto
  Fussar" (fr.txt): Histoire, Interactions, Anecdote.
- Mission pages: "The Gilded Cage" (chapter 4, givers Hosea and Dutch), "Welcome to the New World", "Savagery
  Unleashed" (via the wiki page "Guarma"), "A Kind and Benevolent Despot", "Hell Hath No Fury", "Paradise Mercifully
  Departed" (all chapter 5). The wiki has no "/dialogues" page for any of these missions (Oct 2026).
- TRANSCRIPT: "Red Dead Redemption 2 Full Transcript", Game Scripts Wiki (game-scripts-wiki.blogspot.com), fan
  transcript of the cutscenes and mission dialogue, saved as scripts/v3/work/fussar/fc/gsw.txt (not committed). Scenes
  read in full: "The Gilded Cage" (Bronte on the balcony), "Welcome to the New World" (Levi Simon, Leon Fuentes,
  Hercule Fontaine), "Savagery Unleashed", "A Kind and Benevolent Despot", "Hell Hath No Fury", "Paradise Mercifully
  Departed". Speaker labels are used as given; stage directions (bracketed, fan-written) are used only where a wiki
  page or screenshot agrees.
- Wiki gallery screenshots of the character page, downloaded through the wiki API and viewed (fc/FussarCanon.png,
  fc/FussarStandoff.png, fc/FussarDeath.png): Fussar loading a large wheeled cannon at the top of the tower; Fussar
  aiming a revolver in the cabin; the tower top exploding around the cannon.
- Wiki pages "Guarma", "Aguasdulces", "Cuban Military", "Guarma Rebels", "Levi Simon", "Hercule Fontaine", "Leon
  Fuentes", "JD McKnight".
- Newspapers (wiki article pages, text quoted verbatim): "Guarma Island Sugar Boom" (Blackwater Ledger No. 67, New
  Hanover Gazette No. 32, Saint Denis Times No. 48; published in chapter 4, as in leviticus_B); "Leader of Guarma
  Assassinated" (Blackwater Ledger No. 68, New Hanover Gazette No. 33, Saint Denis Times No. 49); "Unrest in the Tropics"
  (Blackwater Ledger No. 74, New Hanover Gazette No. 39, Saint Denis Times No. 55, the epilogue issue that also carries
  "Bureau of Investigation Founded", as in edgar_A).
- Fact-checked parts aligned with: angelo_A (Bronte names Fussar at the party), leviticus_B (the sugar-boom article),
  arthur_C, dutch_B, javier_A/B/C, bill_A, micah_A/B (Guarma chapter), arthur_E (Fussar among the deaths the story
  imposes on Arthur). HOUSE_FACTS: "Ch. 5, Guarma: Fussar IS killed by Arthur at the cannon."

VERIFIED POINTS
- Bronte points Fussar out on the balcony at the mayor's party and says he owns a sugar plantation on "the island" and
  comes to the city to indulge himself (transcript). In "A Kind and Benevolent Despot" Arthur remembers that Bronte
  pointed him out; Dutch agrees he knew the name (transcript).
- Levi Simon introduces himself as Fussar's "Senior Overseer" and gives the plantation's rank in the Northern Caribbean
  (transcript). Hercule calls him "Colonel Fussar" and Aguasdulces "Fussar's compound" (transcript).
- In Aguasdulces, Fussar questions Javier, who claims to come from Mexico; a soldier punches Javier; Simon is present;
  Fussar later speaks to his men about how America deals with striking workers (transcript; his lines are quoted in
  part B and only paraphrased here).
- Hercule: Fussar knows who the gang are and the price on their heads, and has called in the navy from Cuba (transcript).
  Micah: Fussar holds the ship's captain and has gun positions around the port (transcript).
- Standoff in the cabin, the captain shooting Simon, Fussar firing and running, Dutch missing him (transcript, mission
  page). Fussar at a CANNON in the tower: transcript stage direction ("Fussar loads the cannon"), Hercule's "He's
  shooting", the character page and its gallery screenshot (FussarCanon). The mission page's "Gatling Gun" and the
  Guarma page's "machine gun" are contradicted by the screenshot: not used. Arthur fires a second cannon and destroys the
  top of the tower with Fussar (transcript, character page, HOUSE_FACTS). The mission page adds that Arthur can also
  kill him with a gunshot: given with attribution.

EXCLUDED (one line each)
- Birth in Cuba and service in the Spanish army before 1898 (wiki inference from the medals, sourced to a Reddit post).
- The rank "colonel in the Cuban Military" as a career path ("transferred his allegiance", "rose to the rank"): no source.
- "Anyone opposing him would be tortured and executed": kept only as a Red Dead Wiki claim, next to what the missions show.
- The character page's readings of his character ("open delight", "arrogant and prideful", "pleasure in pain"):
  interpretation; part B owns personality.
- Hercule (and Dutch) drawing Fussar's fire so Arthur can reach the cannon: character page only, no line in the
  transcript (dutch_B dropped it after fact-check); kept as a Red Dead Wiki claim for Hercule only.
- Fussar escaping "through a window" (live v2 page): no source.
- The wiki trivia's reading that Guarma is "even worse" after his death: the 1907 article makes no comparison with Fussar.
- The wiki trivia's parallel with Agustin Allende: interpretation (also dropped in allende_C).
- San Juan Hill being fought on Guarma in the game ("President Congratulates America", Guarma page trivia): about the
  island, not Fussar.
- Dutch's line in "Just a Social Call" that Cornwall's sugar business is destroying the people of Guarma: about Cornwall
  (leviticus fiche), not Fussar.
- Arthur giving Cornwall's name to Angel in "Savagery Unleashed": Cornwall's fiche; Angel is linked to Fussar only by the
  wiki page "Cuban Military".
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no date or place of birth for Alberto Fussar and say nothing of his early life or of how he came to power. By 1899 he governs Guarma, a Caribbean island that [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] places second to the east of Cuba, and he holds the rank of colonel: the smuggler [[hercule-fontaine|Hercule Fontaine]] calls him \"Colonel Fussar\". His seat is Aguasdulces, which Hercule calls Fussar's compound. According to the Red Dead Wiki, the soldiers stationed on Guarma belong to the Cuban military and serve under his command, guarding the plantations and putting down the uprising.",
              "Les jeux ne donnent ni date ni lieu de naissance pour Alberto Fussar, et ne disent rien de sa jeunesse ni de la façon dont il est arrivé au pouvoir. En 1899, il gouverne Guarma, une île des Caraïbes que [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] situe comme la deuxième à l'est de Cuba, et il porte le grade de colonel : le contrebandier [[hercule-fontaine|Hercule Fontaine]] l'appelle \"Colonel Fussar\". Il siège à Aguasdulces, qu'Hercule appelle le domaine de Fussar. D'après le Red Dead Wiki, les soldats présents à Guarma appartiennent à l'armée cubaine et obéissent à ses ordres : ils gardent les plantations et répriment le soulèvement.")},
    {"p": two("Sugar is the island's business. Fussar's overseer, Levi Simon, tells the castaways that they run the third most productive sugar plantation in the Northern Caribbean, and that his employer has many powerful friends. The rebel Leon Fuentes describes the plantation workers as little more than slaves brought in from other islands, worked until they die so that Fussar grows rich. Hercule adds that Leon wants the population to rise against Fussar, but that most people are too frightened. According to the Red Dead Wiki, those who oppose the governor are tortured and put to death, and the harshness of his rule is what set off the rebellion on the island.",
              "L'île vit du sucre. Levi Simon, le contremaître de Fussar, explique aux naufragés qu'ils exploitent la troisième plantation sucrière la plus productive du nord des Caraïbes, et que son patron a beaucoup d'amis puissants. Le rebelle Leon Fuentes décrit les ouvriers de la plantation comme de quasi-esclaves amenés d'autres îles, que l'on fait travailler jusqu'à la mort pour enrichir Fussar. Hercule ajoute que Leon voudrait voir la population se soulever contre Fussar, mais que la plupart des gens ont trop peur. Selon le Red Dead Wiki, ceux qui s'opposent au gouverneur sont torturés puis exécutés, et c'est la dureté de son régime qui a déclenché la rébellion sur l'île.")},
    {"p": two("His sugar sells in the United States. The article \"Guarma Island Sugar Boom\" (Blackwater Ledger No. 67, New Hanover Gazette No. 32, Saint Denis Times No. 48), published in chapter 4, runs under the subheading \"CUBAN IMPORTS ON THE RISE\". It reports that [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]] made two trips to the region to tour sugar plantations and signed an exclusive purchase order with its governor, whom he called \"a great friend of America\". The same article gives the other side: \"Detractors call Fussar a controversial figure who is flamboyant at times and cruel at others and has Guarma under a quasi-military rule.\" It adds that \"His security force is reportedly feared across the island, with plantation workers often working 14 hour shifts to keep up.\"",
              "Son sucre se vend aux États-Unis. L'article \"Guarma Island Sugar Boom\" (Blackwater Ledger n° 67, New Hanover Gazette n° 32, Saint Denis Times n° 48), paru au chapitre 4, porte le sous-titre \"CUBAN IMPORTS ON THE RISE\" (les importations cubaines en hausse). On y lit que [[leviticus-cornwall|Leviticus Cornwall]] s'est rendu deux fois dans la région pour visiter des plantations sucrières et a signé une commande d'achat exclusive avec son gouverneur, qu'il a qualifié de \"a great friend of America\" (un grand ami de l'Amérique). L'article donne aussi la version des opposants : \"Detractors call Fussar a controversial figure who is flamboyant at times and cruel at others and has Guarma under a quasi-military rule.\" (Ses détracteurs voient en Fussar un personnage controversé, tantôt flamboyant, tantôt cruel, qui tient Guarma sous un régime quasi militaire.) Il précise que \"His security force is reportedly feared across the island, with plantation workers often working 14 hour shifts to keep up.\" (Sa force de sécurité serait crainte dans toute l'île, et les ouvriers des plantations font souvent des journées de 14 heures pour suivre la cadence.)")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},
    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("Fussar's first appearance is at the garden party given by Mayor Henri Lemieux at his mansion in Saint Denis, in \"The Gilded Cage\". [[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]], who has invited the gang, receives Dutch and [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] on a balcony and runs through the guests for them. After the mayor, he picks out Fussar. Bronte says that Fussar owns a sugar plantation on the island and comes to the city to indulge himself, and Dutch laughs with him. Fussar says nothing in the scene. Bronte moves on to Hobart Crawley, to Rains Fall and Eagle Flies, and to the newspaperman Hector Fellowes.",
              "Fussar apparaît pour la première fois à la garden-party que le maire Henri Lemieux donne dans sa demeure de Saint-Denis, dans \"The Gilded Cage\". [[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]], qui a invité la bande, reçoit Dutch et [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] sur un balcon et leur passe les invités en revue. Après le maire, il désigne Fussar. Bronte explique que Fussar possède une plantation de sucre sur l'île et qu'il vient en ville pour s'y livrer à la débauche, ce qui fait rire Dutch. Fussar ne prononce pas un mot dans la scène. Bronte passe ensuite à Hobart Crawley, à Rains Fall et Eagle Flies, puis au patron de presse Hector Fellowes.")},
    {"p": two("At the end of chapter 4, after the failed robbery of the Saint Denis bank, Dutch, Arthur, [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] escape on a ship that sinks in a storm. The five men wash up on Guarma, Fussar's island.",
              "À la fin du chapitre 4, après l'échec du braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis, Dutch, Arthur, [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]], [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] s'enfuient sur un navire qui sombre dans une tempête. Les cinq hommes échouent sur Guarma, l'île de Fussar.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 5: Guarma", "Chapitre 5 : Guarma"), "chapter": 5},
    {"p": two("Fussar is first a name. In \"Welcome to the New World\", soldiers led by Levi Simon chain the castaways together on the beach. Simon presents himself as Fussar's senior overseer and speaks of labor troubles and of Haitian pirates who will soon be hanged in the streets. Dutch gives a false name and Simon promises to free the five men once he knows who they are. Hercule Fontaine's rebels ambush the column. Javier is shot in the leg and taken, while the others escape with Hercule, who warns them that Fussar will be desperate to find them. He points out Aguasdulces and the factory where the island's cane is processed. Fussar's men are hunting a group of workers who escaped into the jungle the day before; in \"Savagery Unleashed\", Arthur and Leon Fuentes save some of them from the gallows.",
              "Fussar n'est d'abord qu'un nom. Dans \"Welcome to the New World\", des soldats menés par Levi Simon enchaînent les naufragés sur la plage. Simon se présente comme le contremaître principal de Fussar et parle de troubles chez les ouvriers et de pirates haïtiens qui seront bientôt pendus dans les rues. Dutch donne un faux nom, et Simon promet de libérer les cinq hommes dès qu'il saura qui ils sont. Les rebelles d'Hercule Fontaine attaquent la colonne. Javier, touché à la jambe, est capturé, tandis que les autres s'enfuient avec Hercule, qui les prévient que Fussar remuera ciel et terre pour les retrouver. Il leur montre Aguasdulces et l'usine où l'on traite la canne de l'île. Les hommes de Fussar traquent un groupe d'ouvriers qui s'est enfui dans la jungle la veille ; dans \"Savagery Unleashed\", Arthur et Leon Fuentes en sauvent plusieurs de la potence.")},
    {"p": two("He appears in person in \"A Kind and Benevolent Despot\". On the way through the caves to Aguasdulces, Arthur asks whether Fussar was not one of the men Bronte showed them at the party in Saint Denis, and Dutch agrees that he knew the name. At the top of the ladder, the two men see Fussar arrive with his soldiers and Simon, dragging the captured Javier behind a donkey. Fussar asks Javier who he is; Javier answers that he comes from Mexico and has never met the other men. Fussar mocks him in front of his soldiers, one of whom punches Javier in the face, then leaves him with a parting jibe about Mexicans.",
              "Il apparaît en personne dans \"A Kind and Benevolent Despot\". En chemin vers Aguasdulces, à travers les grottes, Arthur demande si Fussar n'était pas l'un des hommes que Bronte leur a montrés à la réception de Saint-Denis, et Dutch confirme que le nom lui disait quelque chose. En haut de l'échelle, les deux hommes voient arriver Fussar, ses soldats et Simon, qui traînent Javier, prisonnier, derrière un âne. Fussar demande à Javier qui il est ; Javier répond qu'il vient du Mexique et n'a jamais vu les autres hommes. Fussar se moque de lui devant ses soldats, dont l'un frappe Javier au visage, puis le quitte sur une pique au sujet des Mexicains.")},
    {"p": two("While Dutch and Arthur creep around the compound, Fussar can be heard addressing his men in Spanish. He tells them he has just been in America, describes how strikers are dealt with there, and holds it up as the order he wants on Guarma. Meanwhile his soldiers threaten Javier with broken kneecaps to make him talk, and Javier keeps repeating that he knows nothing; according to the Red Dead Wiki, he never gives the gang away. He is held in a cage. Dutch and Arthur kill the guards inside the refinery, spill the sugar from its sacks and set off the furnace. The building explodes, they take Javier from his cage and fight their way out through the cane fields. Fussar is not seen again in the mission.",
              "Pendant que Dutch et Arthur contournent le domaine, on entend Fussar haranguer ses hommes en espagnol. Il leur raconte qu'il revient d'Amérique, leur décrit le sort qu'on y réserve aux grévistes et présente cet exemple comme l'ordre qu'il veut faire régner à Guarma. Ses soldats, eux, menacent Javier de lui briser les rotules pour le faire parler, et Javier répète qu'il ne sait rien ; selon le Red Dead Wiki, il ne trahit jamais la bande. On le garde dans une cage. Dutch et Arthur éliminent les gardes de la raffinerie, répandent le sucre des sacs et font exploser le four. Le bâtiment saute, ils sortent Javier de sa cage et se frayent un chemin à travers les champs de canne. Fussar ne reparaît plus de la mission.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Hell Hath No Fury\", the gang joins Hercule at the old fort of Cinco Torres. Hercule tells Dutch that Fussar now knows who they are and what price is on their heads. If they can silence him, Hercule says, he can get them away before anyone arrives from America; but Fussar has called in the navy from Cuba, and no boat can leave for now. A warship appears in the bay and lands soldiers below the fort. When one of its shells falls among its own men, Dutch thanks Fussar aloud. Arthur asks how many men Fussar has; Hercule answers that the number does not matter, because Fussar has the money to hire more. Arthur sinks the warship with the fort's cannon, and Hercule announces that a boat is on its way.",
              "Dans \"Hell Hath No Fury\", la bande rejoint Hercule au vieux fort de Cinco Torres. Hercule apprend à Dutch que Fussar sait désormais qui ils sont et quelle prime pèse sur leurs têtes. S'ils parviennent à le faire taire, explique Hercule, il pourra les faire partir avant que quiconque n'arrive d'Amérique ; mais Fussar a fait venir la marine de Cuba, et aucun bateau ne peut quitter l'île pour l'instant. Un navire de guerre surgit dans la baie et débarque des soldats au pied du fort. Quand l'un de ses obus tombe au milieu de ses propres hommes, Dutch remercie Fussar à voix haute. Arthur demande combien d'hommes Fussar a sous ses ordres ; Hercule répond que le nombre n'a pas d'importance, puisque Fussar a de quoi en payer d'autres. Arthur coule le navire avec le canon du fort, et Hercule annonce qu'un bateau est en route.")},
    {"p": two("At the start of \"Paradise Mercifully Departed\", Micah comes back from scouting with bad news: Fussar knows exactly who they are and wants to keep them on the island for a few more days. His men hold the ship's captain, and gun positions cover the harbor so that any boat trying to sail will be shot to pieces. Hercule declares that he will fight Fussar every day he can. Bill stays on the ship with the recovering Javier, while Dutch, Arthur, Micah and Hercule blow up the coastal guns with dynamite and fight their way into Aguasdulces, where the captain is held in a blue building.",
              "Au début de \"Paradise Mercifully Departed\", Micah revient de reconnaissance avec de mauvaises nouvelles : Fussar sait exactement qui ils sont et veut les retenir sur l'île quelques jours de plus. Ses hommes détiennent le capitaine du navire, et des pièces d'artillerie couvrent le port, de sorte que tout bateau qui tenterait de prendre la mer serait criblé d'obus. Hercule déclare qu'il combattra Fussar chaque jour qu'il pourra. Bill reste à bord avec Javier, encore convalescent, tandis que Dutch, Arthur, Micah et Hercule font sauter les canons de la côte à la dynamite et se frayent un chemin jusqu'à Aguasdulces, où le capitaine est retenu dans un bâtiment bleu.")},
    {"p": two("Inside the cabin, Simon is lying in wait; he knocks Arthur to the floor and holds him at gunpoint. Dutch walks in and aims at Simon. Fussar then walks in, revolver drawn, and tells them they are going to die; Dutch draws his second revolver to cover him, and Arthur aims at Fussar from the floor. Fussar warns that the United States Navy is on its way. Dutch answers that this is exactly why Fussar will let them leave, or die where he stands. Arthur pushes a rifle lying on the floor over to the captain, who shoots Simon in the chest and kills him. Fussar fires a few shots and runs out of the cabin; moments later Dutch asks whether he has escaped.",
              "Dans la cabane, Simon attend Arthur ; il le jette à terre et le tient en joue. Dutch entre et braque Simon. Fussar entre alors, revolver au poing, et leur annonce qu'ils vont mourir ; Dutch tire son second revolver pour le tenir en respect, et Arthur, toujours à terre, le met en joue. Fussar prévient que la marine des États-Unis est en route. Dutch répond que c'est justement pour cela que Fussar va les laisser partir, ou mourir sur place. Arthur pousse vers le capitaine un fusil qui traîne au sol, et le capitaine abat Simon d'une balle en pleine poitrine. Fussar tire quelques coups de feu et s'enfuit de la cabane ; un instant plus tard, Dutch demande s'il s'est échappé.")},
    {"p": two("The group runs for the ship through Fussar's soldiers. Near the port, Hercule spots Fussar at the top of a tower, where he loads a cannon and opens fire on them. Hercule sends Arthur to a second cannon on the ground, further ahead on the left; according to the Red Dead Wiki, Hercule draws Fussar's fire so that Arthur can reach it. Arthur fires at the tower and blows its top apart, killing Fussar. According to the mission page, Arthur can also kill him with a gunshot instead of the cannon. Arthur remarks that he got Fussar for Javier. The captain takes the five gang members on board, Hercule says the rebels will probably disappear back to Haiti, and the ship sails for America. Fussar dies in 1899.",
              "Le groupe court vers le navire à travers les soldats de Fussar. Près du port, Hercule repère Fussar au sommet d'une tour, où il charge un canon et ouvre le feu sur eux. Hercule envoie Arthur vers un second canon, au sol, un peu plus loin sur la gauche ; selon le Red Dead Wiki, Hercule attire sur lui les tirs de Fussar pour permettre à Arthur de l'atteindre. Arthur tire sur la tour et en fait voler le sommet en éclats, tuant Fussar. D'après la page de la mission, Arthur peut aussi l'abattre d'un coup de feu au lieu d'utiliser le canon. Arthur lance qu'il a eu Fussar pour Javier. Le capitaine embarque les cinq membres de la bande, Hercule annonce que les rebelles vont sans doute disparaître et repartir en Haïti, et le navire met le cap sur l'Amérique. Fussar meurt en 1899.")},
    {"p": two("Back in the United States, a later issue of the papers (Blackwater Ledger No. 68, New Hanover Gazette No. 33, Saint Denis Times No. 49) carries the article \"Leader of Guarma Assassinated\", headed \"ALBERTO FUSSAR DEAD.\" and \"BELOVED LEADER CUT DOWN.\" It states that \"Reports conflict as to the details of his demise, though early assumptions are that it was part of an attempted coup.\" It reports that American business leaders \"speak warmly of Mr. Fussar as a kind and effective leader who brought peace and prosperity to the region, supported workers' rights, and took a particular interest in the lot of women on the island.\" The killing was first blamed on a revolt of the plantation workers, but \"reports have begun to reach the mainland that several white men were involved in the assassination\", and some blame a band of socialist insurrectionists. Some locals, according to the article, say tensions had grown as working conditions worsened under American pressure for cheaper sugar.",
              "De retour aux États-Unis, un numéro ultérieur des journaux (Blackwater Ledger n° 68, New Hanover Gazette n° 33, Saint Denis Times n° 49) publie l'article \"Leader of Guarma Assassinated\", titré \"ALBERTO FUSSAR DEAD.\" (Alberto Fussar est mort) et \"BELOVED LEADER CUT DOWN.\" (un dirigeant bien-aimé abattu). On y lit que \"Reports conflict as to the details of his demise, though early assumptions are that it was part of an attempted coup.\" (les récits de sa mort se contredisent, mais les premières hypothèses évoquent une tentative de coup d'État). Selon l'article, les milieux d'affaires américains \"speak warmly of Mr. Fussar as a kind and effective leader who brought peace and prosperity to the region, supported workers' rights, and took a particular interest in the lot of women on the island.\" (parlent chaleureusement de M. Fussar comme d'un dirigeant bienveillant et efficace, qui a apporté paix et prospérité à la région, soutenu les droits des ouvriers et s'est particulièrement soucié du sort des femmes de l'île). Le meurtre a d'abord été imputé à une révolte des ouvriers des plantations, mais \"reports have begun to reach the mainland that several white men were involved in the assassination\" (des informations parvenues sur le continent font état de l'implication de plusieurs hommes blancs), et certains accusent une bande d'insurgés socialistes. Des habitants, ajoute l'article, attribuent les tensions à la dégradation des conditions de travail, les importateurs américains exigeant un sucre toujours moins cher.")},

    # ================================================================ Epilogue 1907
    {"h3": two("After his death: the epilogue (1907)", "Après sa mort : l'épilogue (1907)"), "year": "1907"},
    {"p": two("Fussar is mentioned once more in the newspapers of the epilogue period (Blackwater Ledger No. 74, New Hanover Gazette No. 39, Saint Denis Times No. 55). The article \"Unrest in the Tropics\", headed \"COST OF FOOD, FUEL ANGERS CITIZENS.\", describes soaring prices and shortages from Barbados to Cuba. It recalls \"the assassination of prominent sugar industry advocate and Guarman governor Alberto Fussar in 1899\". It reports that, shortly afterwards, American banking institutions, JD McKnight and Co. among them, took control of the sugar industry on several islands, Guarma included. Fields that once fed the islanders were turned over to sugar cane, so that all food has to be imported at great expense. The foreign investors hire locals to guard their plantations, \"subjecting workers to harsh conditions and penalties\". According to the Red Dead Wiki, McKnight's company also took over many of Cornwall's businesses.",
              "Fussar est cité une dernière fois dans les journaux de la période de l'épilogue (Blackwater Ledger n° 74, New Hanover Gazette n° 39, Saint Denis Times n° 55). L'article \"Unrest in the Tropics\", titré \"COST OF FOOD, FUEL ANGERS CITIZENS.\" (le prix de la nourriture et du combustible exaspère la population), décrit l'envolée des prix et les pénuries de la Barbade à Cuba. Il rappelle \"the assassination of prominent sugar industry advocate and Guarman governor Alberto Fussar in 1899\" (l'assassinat en 1899 d'Alberto Fussar, gouverneur de Guarma et ardent défenseur de l'industrie sucrière). Il rapporte que peu après, des établissements bancaires américains, dont JD McKnight and Co., ont pris le contrôle de l'industrie sucrière de plusieurs îles, dont Guarma. Les champs qui nourrissaient les habitants ont été convertis à la canne à sucre, si bien que toute la nourriture doit être importée à grands frais. Les investisseurs étrangers emploient des gens du pays pour garder leurs plantations, \"subjecting workers to harsh conditions and penalties\" (en soumettant les ouvriers à des conditions et à des sanctions sévères). Selon le Red Dead Wiki, la société de McKnight a aussi repris une bonne partie des affaires de Cornwall.")},
]
